        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A successful <strong class="text-white">DIY epoxy garage floor</strong> is decided before any resin is mixed. Test the slab for moisture with a taped-down sheet of plastic, grind rather than acid-etch to open the surface, and degrease every oil stain until the concrete underneath is clean.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Then work to the clock rather than to the eye: mix one batch at a time within its pot life, respect the recoat window between coats, and keep the car off for the full seven-day cure. Every common failure — peeling, fisheyes, tyre pickup — comes from skipping one of those steps, not from the product.
          </p>
